WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.538
SQL includes different groups of commands and it
helps to know what

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:09.525
job each group performs DDL stands for Data
Definition Language These

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:14.262
commands define or change the structure of the
database CREATE can create

00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:20.638
a table or another database object ALTER changes an
existing structure DROP

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.225
removes an object TRUNCATE removes rows from a table
while keeping the

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:29.575
table itself We worked more with this type of SQL
when designing

00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:35.488
the database DQL is commonly used to describe Data
Query Language The

00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:40.188
key command here is SELECT SELECT reads data and
builds a result

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:44.512
set Most of the first half of this module focuses on
querying

00:00:44.538 --> 00:00:50.500
data with SELECT DML stands for Data Manipulation
Language INSERT

00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:54.912
adds rows UPDATE changes rows DELETE removes rows
and MERGE can synchronize

00:00:54.925 --> 00:01:00.125
source and target data under defined conditions We
also have transaction control

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.950
BEGIN starts a transaction COMMIT keeps the changes
ROLLBACK discards

00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:11.425
the changes made inside the transaction You do not
need to memorize

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:17.125
the abbreviations Focus on the purpose Some SQL
defines structure

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:20.700
some reads data some changes data and some controls
whether a group

00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:24.988
of changes is kept or undone The schema from Module
2 provides

00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:28.712
the rules and the statements in this module operate
inside those rules
